  "description": "Perseverance and Curiosity's newest raw images from NASA: the latest 24 of each as image grids, and of the newest 100 which cameras took them and on which sol (a Mars day). Statistics: a rate needs an exposure. The same 100 images can cover one sol or many, so images per sol divides by the sols the window spans, including sols with none, with a Poisson 95% interval; per sol with images it would be a different number. Caveats: the window is cut by count, so its first sol is partly missing and its newest sols are still being downlinked; images come in bursts (mosaics, drives), so the Poisson interval is too narrow.",
